  "pr_number": 4567,
  "issue_number": 427,
  "issue_title": "feat(discovery): add trust filter counts and quick chips to browse",
  "issue_body": "## Goal\nMake browse trust filters easier to use by adding visible quick filter chips and result counts for the existing trust-related filters.\n\n## Why this matters\nHeyClaude already has useful trust metadata, but visitors need faster ways to discover safe/source-backed/verified resources. A clearer filter UI should make the directory feel more like a product and less like a raw list.\n\n## Current behavior\n`/browse` already supports trust-related filters through the utility filter select, including safety notes, privacy notes, source-backed entries, trusted packages, reviewed entries, checksums, and prerequisites. These filters are currently hidden inside one utility dropdown and do not show counts before selection.\n\n## Desired behavior\nAdd a compact trust/filter strip near the browse search controls that exposes the most useful trust filters as quick chips with counts:\n\n- Safety notes\n- Privacy notes\n- Source-backed\n- Trusted package\n- Reviewed/claimed\n- Checksums\n\nThe existing utility dropdown should continue to work. Selecting a chip should update the same filter state and URL behavior as the existing controls.\n\n## Scope\n- Browse directory UI and existing browse URL state only.\n- Reuse existing registry fields already loaded by the browse page.\n- Add or update focused tests for filter behavior if existing tests cover this area.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Do not redesign the full browse page.\n- Do not change content schemas or generated registry artifacts.\n- Do not add server-side search infrastructure.\n- Do not add multiple simultaneous trust filters in this issue unless it falls out naturally without broad refactoring.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The quick filter strip shows counts computed from the currently loaded entries.\n- Clicking a trust chip applies the corresponding existing utility filter.\n- URL sync still works for selected filters.\n- Empty states remain clear and polished.\n- The PR includes `Closes #<this issue number>`.\n\n## Validation\nRun from the repo root:\n\n```sh\npnpm exec vitest run tests/discovery-surfaces.test.ts\npnpm build\ngit diff --check\n```\n\n## Contributor note\nThis repository is listed on Gittensor; eligibility and rewards follow Gittensor's current rules. We do not promise rewards from this issue.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-07T14:26:46.000Z",
